{"id": "EUVD-2026-95795", "enisaUuid": "251fad6a-0ee7-3383-921a-99785510c0e0", "description": "Open5GS through 2.8.0 contains a reachable assertion vulnerability in mme_gn_handle_sgsn_context_request() that allows remote unauthenticated attackers to crash the MME via malformed SGSN Address IEs. Attackers sending GTPv1-C traffic from a configured SGSN address with a known UE IMSI or P-TMSI can supply an invalid address length to terminate open5gs-mmed, denying service to all subscribers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T14:08:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T17:29:06", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/commit/346ce7a5e5cf2812bac3af042b5afba35bcf4f89", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/security/advisories/GHSA-9crh-64c8-56q6", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/blob/v2.8.0/src/mme/mme-gn-handler.c#L208-L217", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/open5gs-through-2.8.0-mme-reachable-assertion-via-gtpv1-sgsn-context-request"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ch22-9c64-r8wh", "CVE-2026-108105"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b5b6b6e-e567-38a9-9203-9792a1c5d8ef", "product": {"name": "Open5GS", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0441f27c-1f9f-35a8-b271-68879c2238a0", "vendor": {"name": "Open5GS"}}], "isExploited": false}